  "worked_solution": "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(-2,0,1)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=\u27e83,4,-2\u27e9.$ Therefore, its vector equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\u27e8-2,0,1\u27e9+t\u27e83,4,-2\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-2+3t,4t,1-2t\u27e9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $r=\u27e8-2+3t,4t,1-2t\u27e9$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot \u27e84,-3,1\u27e9 & =-9 \\\\ \u27e8-2+3t,4t,1-2t\u27e9\\cdot \u27e84,-3,1\u27e9 & =-9 \\\\ 4(-2+3t)-3(4t)+(1-2t) & =-9 \\\\ -8+12t-12t+1-2t & =-9 \\\\ -2t & =-2 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=1$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =\u27e8-2+3(1),4(1),1-2(1)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e81,4,-1\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(1,4,-1).$",
